    565	### C9 — Pointwise Ramanujan-spike approximator T_Q(n) — **BUILT (S191, paradigm-shift mode)**
    566	**Edges:** E2.1 + E1.5 + E1.6 + E2.2 + S168.
    567	**Object:** `T_Q(n) := (π(N)/N) · Σ_{q sqf ≤ Q} mu(gcd(q,n)) / phi(q/gcd(q,n))` — pointwise dual of S168's energy-level spike formula, computable in `O(Q·ω(n))` per evaluation. Falsifiers: (PR1) `||T_Q − const||² / π(N)` at Q=N^{0.185}, d=20 in [0.18, 0.26] (matches S169 SVD spike block). (PR2) Pearson(chi_P, T_Q) monotone-increasing in Q. (PR3) Precision-at-π(N) > Q · π(N)/N. (PR4) Hölder identity `mu(q) c_q(n)/phi(q) = mu(gcd)/phi(q/gcd)` exact for sqf q ≤ 30, n ≤ 60.
    568	**Outcome (S191):** All four falsifiers PASS. At d=20, Q=13: ratio = 0.2229 (matches S169's 0.220 to 1.4%). Precision lift 5.6× at Q=N^{0.185}, scaling to 12.8× at Q=√N. **Wheel-Mertens identity**: at primorial Q=W and n coprime to W, `T_W(n) = (π(N)/N) · W/φ(W)`. **Status:** BUILT. No polylog opening (cost is `Q · ω(n) = Ω(N^{0.185})`); structural picture only. EDGES.md E2.1 annotated, CLOSED_PATHS row added. **Save under:** `experiments/constructions/ramanujan_spike_pointwise/`.
